    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d692">

                <pb facs="0621" n="505" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg505"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 814.51/183.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 30, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: With reference to the
                    subject of the Guatemalan debt, as to which I telegraphed to you on September
                    29th giving you the views of my Government, I must thank you for the action
                    taken by you in accordance with the wishes of my Government, as set forth in
                    your note to Mr. Mitchell Innes of September 21st. I need not say that my
                    Government deeply appreciates any assistance from the Government of the United
                    States looking to the satisfaction of British claims of this nature.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">James Bryce.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
